A binding names a value.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    score = 10
    player_name = "Priya"
]

An unannotated numeric origin can stay unresolved while Moth considers eligible
exact uses in its function body. If none resolves it, whole-number bindings
default to `I32` and decimal/exponent bindings to `F64`. Other values keep their
own inferred types.

Write the type when it makes the code clearer or gives the compiler needed
context:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    score I32 = 10
    player_name String = "Priya"
]

Bindings stay immutable unless you mark them as mutable. An immutable binding
can't take a different value later.
